P2.2.1 is done. Here's what was implemented:

**`GET /votes/consensus`** — the route already existed but recomputed on every request by scanning all ~12K votes. Changes made to `votes.service.ts`:

1. Added `ConsensusResult` interface with explicit types
2. Added an in-memory `consensusCache` field (1-hour TTL)  
3. Split `getConsensus()` into a public cache-aware wrapper and a private `computeConsensus()` method
4. Cache hits skip the full DB scan (~12K votes × batches), returning in microseconds
5. Response now includes `computedAt` ISO timestamp so the frontend can show data freshness
6. The existing `Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600` header on the controller handles CDN-level caching on top

TypeScript typechecks clean.
